%% Purpose: Safe two-phase deployment for shared Cosmos and Storage
%% Audience: Platform engineering and operations teams
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant IaC as Deployment automation
    participant Foundry as Foundry project
    participant Cosmos as Shared Cosmos DB
    participant Storage as Shared Storage
    participant Gate as Verification gate

    IaC->>Foundry: Create project, identity, connections, capability host
    IaC->>Cosmos: Grant temporary database-scoped access
    IaC->>Storage: Grant account role with project-prefix condition
    Note over IaC,Storage: Bootstrap window uses synthetic data only, with no user access
    IaC->>Foundry: Invoke one canary agent through Responses API
    Foundry->>Cosmos: Create the two lazy modern containers
    Foundry->>Storage: Create project-prefixed containers
    IaC->>Cosmos: Add five project-container grants
    IaC->>Cosmos: Remove temporary database grant
    IaC->>Gate: Inventory actual grants and container ownership
    Gate->>Cosmos: Own-project ALLOW and cross-project DENY
    Gate->>Storage: Own-project ALLOW and cross-project DENY
    alt Every configuration and behavior check passes
        Gate-->>IaC: Cosmos and Storage verified
        Note over IaC,Gate: User access may now be assigned
    else Any check fails or is network-blocked
        Gate-->>IaC: Fail closed
        Note over IaC,Gate: Environment remains unavailable for real data
    end
